C004JRWFW43H037MQRN". object.client_reference (Required): string or null. The reference the payment link URL or resolve request carried, such as your user ID. `null` when none was sent or checkout did not start from a payment link. Returned only to merchant credentials; omitted for buyer credentials. Set by the buyer's browser, so treat it as a claim, not proof of identity. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. object.closed_at (Optional): string. When the order closed. Present exactly when status is closed. Set once at the transition and never changed. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.closed_reason (Optional): string. Why the order closed. Present exactly when status is closed. Set once at closure. Unrecognized reasons are returned as other; new values may be added. Value enum: "invoice_voided", "paid", "closed_by_merchant", "checkout_expired", "written_off", "superseded", "return_resolution_canceled", "other". object.closed_reason_message (Optional): string. The caller note supplied when closing the order. System closures leave it absent. It is not shown to the buyer. object.created_at (Required): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.custom_field_answers (Required): Array of {@see CustomFieldAnswerInput}. The buyer's answers to the payment link's custom fields, recorded when checkout started, in the order the link showed the fields. Each answer keeps the field's key, label, and type from that moment, so later changes to the link don't change it. Optional fields the buyer left blank are left out. Read-only. Empty when the order didn't come from a payment link, the link had no custom fields, or the buyer answered none. Orders created before Flint recorded answers here also return an empty list and keep their answers in `metadata` as `custom_field_<key>`. Deleting the customer removes the answers. Returned only to merchant credentials; omitted for buyer credentials. maxItems: 20. object.custom_field_a