ession credential that doesn't act for the customer the buyer verified. Where an order is delivered: the address, the recipient, and where the destination came from. object.discounts (Required): Array of {@see OrderDiscountInput}. Discounts applied to the order, each with its amount, status, and the line items and charges it covers. object.discounts[] (Value): {@see OrderDiscountInput}. A discount applied to an order, with its amount, status, and the line items and charges it covers. It comes from a manual discount or a promotion. object.dispute_status (Optional): string. Aggregate dispute state across the order's counted payment intents, excluding payment_returned. Always returned to merchant credentials and omitted from buyer reads. Open states take precedence in this order: needs_response, under_review, inquiry_needs_response, inquiry_under_review, other. Otherwise the most severe closed state wins: lost, won, prevented, inquiry_closed; none when no disputes count. List individual cases with GET /v1/disputes?order_id={order_id}. Value enum: "none", "inquiry_needs_response", "inquiry_under_review", "inquiry_closed", "needs_response", "under_review", "won", "lost", "prevented", "other". object.external_reference_id (Optional): string. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.fulfillment_status (Optional): string. Aggregate progress across the order's fulfillment quantities. Value enum: "not_fulfilled", "partially_fulfilled", "fulfilled", "canceled", "not_applicable", "closed". object.fulfillments (Required): Array of {@see FulfillmentInput}. Fulfillments created for the order, each covering a set of its line items. object.fulfillments[] (Value): {@see FulfillmentInput}. Work required to deliver an order's items. object.gift_card_estimate (Optional): {@see OrderGiftCardEstimateInput}. An estimate of how the order balance splits between gift cards and the payment processor. An estimate of how an order total splits between gift cards and the payment processor, and whether gift cards can pay it. object.gift_card_settlements (Required): Array of {@see OrderGiftCardSettlementInput}. The gift card redemptions applied to the order's payments. object.gift_card_settlements[] (Value): {@see OrderGiftCardSettlementInput}. A gift card redemption applied to an order payment, with the amount, tip, and gift card. object.gift_card_tender_enabled (Required): boolean. Whether gift cards can pay for this order now. Gift cards pay only USD orders that still accept changes, are not subscription purchases, and whose merchant has at least one gift card that is not closed in this environment. Recomputed on each read; a spent but open card still counts. object.gift_cards (Required): Array of {@see OrderGiftCardSelectionInput}. Gift cards available to pay the order, with each card's available balance. object.gift_cards[] (Value): {@see OrderGiftCardSelectionInput}. A gift card available to pay an order, with its available balance and the last four characters of its code. object.governing_delivery_selection_id (Required): string or null. ID of the delivery selection that governs this order, including pickup choices without a delivery destination: the checkout's provisional selection before payment, and the selection a payment committed after. Read it with GET /v1/delivery-selections/{delivery_selection_id}. Null when no selection governs the order. While set, change the destination through the delivery selection. Example: "dsel_01KEZF7C00QC35XBXVXQSCEB2D". object.handover (Optional): {@see OrderHandoverInput}. Carry-out handover: every physical item is handed to the buyer at this location when the order is paid, in place of a delivery selection. Payment then creates one completed `handover` fulfillment. Absent without a handover. Every physical item is handed to the buyer at this location when the order is paid. Replaces a delivery selection. object.internal_note (Optional): string. A note for your team. Buyer reads leave it out. object.inventory_exception_reason (Optional): string. Why inventory could not be committed after payment. The cause remains after resolution. Omitted when no reason was recorded. Unrecognized reasons are returned as other; new values may be added. Value enum: "inventory_deduction_failed", "inventory_handoff_failed", "auto_refund_required", "auto_refund_failed", "policy_resolution_failed", "other". object.inventory_exception_resolution_message (Optional): string. The merchant note supplied when resolving the inventory exception. It is not shown to the buyer. object.inventory_exception_status (Optional): string. Whether an inventory problem after payment needs attention. Value enum: "paid_inventory_failed", "resolved". object.inventory_reservation_id (Optional): string. The reservation holding stock for this order, when one exists. Example: "invr_01KEZF7C0041ENRR0C2NF3AP12". object.inventory_routing_source (Optional): {@see InventoryRoutingSourceInput}. Where this order's tracked demand is routed. Required before an order containing tracked variants can hold stock. Where an order, payment link, or reservation routes inventory from: a fixed Location, an inventory allocation policy, or one policy revision. object.invoice_id (Required): string or null. The invoice associated with this order. Null when the order has no invoice. A replacement invoice replaces this ID; voiding an invoice preserves it. Example: "inv_01KEZF7C00A5GEBMWHEAJFSAR4". object.line_items (Required): Array of {@see OrderLineItemInput}. Items the order sells, each with its pricing, tax, and fulfillment quantities. object.line_items[] (Value): {@see OrderLineItemInput}. An item purchased in an order. object.merchant_id (Required): string. ID of the merchant this resource belongs to. Example: "mer_01KEZF7C00KPYH1DDFPCCX3B6E". object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Stored caller-owned key-value data. See `MetadataInput` for key, value, and s